/S /P
/P 443 0 R
/E (Three random testing approaches were studied for the SwiftRide fare calculation system. Uniform random testing generates inputs from valid ranges, operational-profile testing represents actual passenger usage, and adaptive random testing spreads test inputs across different regions of the input space. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1690 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 443 0 R
/E (The boundary probability calculation shows that only 1% of the distance values lie within 0.1 km of either the 2 km or 10 km boundary. Therefore, random testing alone may not reliably detect boundary-related faults. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
