/E (Final Conclusion )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1692 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 443 0 R
/E (Adaptive random testing is useful for exploring different input combinations, while operational-profile testing is useful for estimating reliability under realistic passenger usage. Uniform random testing provides a simple method for generating a large number of test cases. For SwiftRide, random testing should be used as a supporting technique after applying equivalence class partitioning, boundary value analysis and decision table testing. This combination provides better fault detection and improves confidence in the fare calculation system. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
