4328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (The complete testing process of the SwiftRide Cab Booking and Fare Engine helped demonstrate how software quality can be evaluated using different testing approaches. During the testing activities, different input values, business rules, program conditions, and execution paths were considered. This provided a better understanding of how errors can occur in different parts of an application and how suitable test cases can help identify them. )
/Pg 106 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
4329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (One of the major findings was that testing only the normal working conditions of an application is not sufficient. The system must also be tested with invalid inputs, boundary values, unexpected combinations, and different user actions. For example, in fare calculation, a small difference in travel distance, waiting time, or booking time can affect the final fare. Similarly, an incorrect promotional condition or wallet balance check may result in an incorrect transaction. Therefore, testing different situations is necessary to ensure that the system behaves correctly. )
/Pg 106 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
4330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (Another important finding was that each testing technique provides a different level of understanding of the application. Black-box testing focuses on the expected behaviour of the system, whereas white-box testing examines its internal structure. Boundary Value Analysis is useful for identifying errors around limits, while decision table testing helps verify combinations of business conditions. State transition testing checks whether the booking process follows the correct sequence of operations. Pairwise testing helps reduce the number of test cases when multiple input parameters are involved. )
/Pg 106 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
4331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (The code analysis activities also showed the importance of measuring test effectiveness. Statement and branch coverage indicate how much of the program has been executed, but they do not guarantee that all defects have been detected. Mutation testing provides additional information by checking whether the test cases can identify small changes in the program. Similarly, Control Flow Graphs and Cyclomatic Complexity help understand the program structure and identify independent execution paths that require testing. )
/Pg 106 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
4332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (The comparison of different test suites highlighted the importance of selecting test cases based on risk, functionality, and system complexity. A large number of test cases does not )
/Pg 106 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
