/K [1]
>>
endobj
4335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 513 0 R
/T (Software testing is essential in real-world applications because users expect systems to provide correct and consistent results. In a cab booking application, incorrect fare calculation can create payment problems and reduce customer trust. Incorrect driver searching or booking status updates can also affect the overall user experience. )
/E (Software testing is essential in real-world applications because users expect systems to provide correct and consistent results. In a cab booking application, incorrect fare calculation can create payment problems and reduce customer trust. Incorrect driver searching or booking status updates can also affect the overall user experience. )
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
4336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 513 0 R
/T (automatically mean better testing. Instead, test cases should be meaningful, cover important conditions, and identify possible defects without unnecessary repetition. Combining multiple testing techniques can provide better confidence in the quality of the application. CHALLENGES FACED DURING TESTING )
/E (automatically mean better testing. Instead, test cases should be meaningful, cover important conditions, and identify possible defects without unnecessary repetition. Combining multiple testing techniques can provide better confidence in the quality of the application. CHALLENGES FACED DURING TESTING )
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
4337 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 513 0 R
/T (Several challenges were considered during the testing of the SwiftRide system. One challenge was identifying all the possible combinations of input conditions. The fare engine contains multiple parameters, including distance, waiting time, booking time, promotional codes, payment modes, and wallet balance. Testing every possible combination would require a large number of test cases. Pairwise testing and decision table techniques help manage this complexity. )
/E (Several challenges were considered during the testing of the SwiftRide system. One challenge was identifying all the possible combinations of input conditions. The fare engine contains multiple parameters, including distance, waiting time, booking time, promotional codes, payment modes, and wallet balance. Testing every possible combination would require a large number of test cases. Pairwise testing and decision table techniques help manage this complexity. )
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
4338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 513 0 R
/T (Another challenge was identifying the correct expected output for each test case. Fare calculation involves multiple operations, such as base fare calculation, waiting charges, night surcharges, discounts, and fare limits. The order of these operations can affect the final result. Therefore, the business rules must be clearly understood before preparing expected results. Testing the internal program structure also requires careful analysis. A test suite may execute every statement but still fail to detect certain logical errors. Identifying independent paths, evaluating individual conditions, and analysing surviving mutants require additional effort. It is also important to distinguish equivalent mutants from actual faults because some program changes may not affect the final output. )
/E (Another challenge was identifying the correct expected output for each test case. Fare calculation involves multiple operations, such as base fare calculation, waiting charges, night surcharges, discounts, and fare limits. The order of these operations can affect the final result. Therefore, the business rules must be clearly understood before preparing expected results. Testing the internal program structure also requires careful analysis. A test suite may execute every statement but still fail to detect certain logical errors. Identifying independent paths, evaluating individual conditions, and analysing surviving mutants require additional effort. It is also important to distinguish equivalent mutants from actual faults because some program changes may not affect the final output. )
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
4339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 513 0 R
/T (Changing requirements create another challenge. When new features such as shared rides, surge pricing, loyalty discounts, and additional charges are introduced, existing test cases may no longer be sufficient. The testing team must identify affected areas, update test data, and perform regression testing to ensure that existing functionality continues to work correctly. IMPORTANCE OF TESTING IN REAL-WORLD APPLICATIONS )
/E (Changing requirements create another challenge. When new features such as shared rides, surge pricing, loyalty discounts, and additional charges are introduced, existing test cases may no longer be sufficient. The testing team must identify affected areas, update test data, and perform regression testing to ensure that existing functionality continues to work correctly. IMPORTANCE OF TESTING IN REAL-WORLD APPLICATIONS )
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
