/P 514 0 R
/E (The testing process can be improved further by introducing more automated testing methods. Automated test scripts can execute frequently used test cases and help verify the system after every software update. This can reduce manual work and make regression testing faster. )
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
4347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 514 0 R
/E (The test suite can also be expanded to include performance testing, security testing, and usability testing. Performance testing can evaluate how the system behaves when many users book rides at the same time. Security testing can help identify weaknesses related to user information, payment details, and account access. Usability testing can examine whether users can easily complete the booking and payment process. )
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
4348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 514 0 R
/E (In addition, data-driven testing can be used to execute the same test logic with different sets of input values. Risk-based testing can give higher priority to important features such as fare calculation, payment processing, and booking confirmation. Model-based testing can also help generate test cases from the booking lifecycle and its state transitions. )
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
4349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 514 0 R
/E (Artificial intelligence tools may support test case generation and defect identification. However, generated test cases must be reviewed and validated before they are included in the final test suite. Human understanding of business requirements remains important for ensuring that the expected behaviour is correct. )
/Pg 108 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
