7255 0 obj
<<
/Title (Another challenge was identifying the correct expected output for each test case. Fare calculation involves multiple operations, such as base fare calculation, waiting charges, night surcharges, discounts, and fare limits. The order of these operations can affect the final result. Therefore, the business rules must be clearly understood before preparing expected results. Testing the internal program structure also requires careful analysis. A test suite may execute every statement but still fail to detect certain logical errors. Identifying independent paths, evaluating individual conditions, and analysing surviving mutants require additional effort. It is also important to distinguish equivalent mutants from actual faults because some program changes may not affect the final output.)
/Dest [107 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 7261 0 R
/Next 7248 0 R
>>
endobj
